.TH "PB-ENV-VAULT-RESET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-vault-reset - Replace personal ENV keys and delete every personal value


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env vault reset [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Replace personal ENV keys and delete every personal value

.PP
Replace personal ENV keys and delete every personal value after exact account confirmation. This is destructive and differs from local lock, remove, or password change.

.PP
The local vault protects ENV key custody with a password and optional recovery code. Locking clears unlocked keys from this device; removing local custody differs from resetting and deleting account values. Never place a password or recovery code in shell arguments.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	exact confirmation phrase: RESET ENV <account_id>

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for reset

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--password-file\fP=""
	read the raw master password from an absolute owner-only file

.PP
\fB--password-stdin\fP[=false]
	read the raw master password from non-interactive stdin

.PP
\fB--recovery-file\fP=""
	save a newly generated recovery code to a new absolute file path


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env-vault(1)\fP
